.cpcache/
.clj-kondo/.cache/
.claude/

# The walker runs from a checkout, against a database and with a key, so this is
# the repo that invites a stray cookbook-seal.key at its root. A leaked password
# can be rotated; a leaked key cannot, and there is no reset — see README, "Where
# the key comes from". Named here so that `git add -A` cannot pick one up.
*.key

# And, for the same reason, a copy of a database pulled down to be migrated.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# `make dist` — the flattened, self-contained scripts. Built artifacts, and the
# two that carry credentials are baked from them by the private deploy script,
# so a staged one is a step away from holding passwords.
target/
